{"requirements":[{"id":"R1","requirement":"On node1, serve a package repository whose packages and metadata reside on local storage.","status":"satisfied","summary":"A tree RPM and generated repository metadata were stored under /var/www/html/localrepo. Apache was enabled and active, and the repository metadata returned HTTP 200. Post-restart evidence again showed the local files, listener, active service, and HTTP 200 response.","evidence_ids":["cmd-2868bfce52564df1","cmd-60754ad97be44b53","cmd-e68c1694ff804708","cmd-bc82d9431e134b26"]},{"id":"R2","requirement":"Install a package from the local repository while the usual remote repositories are unavailable to the transaction.","status":"satisfied","summary":"Tree was initially absent. The successful cache-refreshed installation disabled every repository except local-offline and disabled subscription-manager repository injection; DNF identified local-offline as the package source, completed the installation, and the executable ran successfully.","evidence_ids":["cmd-27cf3e80f2524dd8","cmd-5c9d78a2402d4e09"]}],"confidence":0.98,"operational_hygiene":{"score":0.98,"summary":"State-changing actions were causally related to installing repository prerequisites, creating and serving the repository, proving a local-only installation, correcting the timed-out installation attempt, or executing the mandatory restart protocol. The failed dead-proxy attempt cleared DNF caches for the intended offline test but did not install tree; terminating its lingering processes was appropriate cleanup. The only unnecessary retained residue observed was /tmp/benchmark-reboot.log, created by the restart command and left after reboot. No failed services or package inconsistency was observed after execution.","evidence_ids":["cmd-d0c6302e748a492d","cmd-2868bfce52564df1","cmd-60754ad97be44b53","cmd-9ab69a5dd7724f11","cmd-508bdc67eb8c4051","cmd-5c9d78a2402d4e09","cmd-a020b16d44c840c6","global:after_executor:node1:temporary-files","global:after_executor:node1:failed-services","global:after_executor:node1:package-health"]},"overall_summary":"Both material task outcomes are satisfied. The independent restart protocol is also complete: it captured a healthy pre-restart repository and installed package, acknowledged the restart, observed a different boot ID, and verified recovered system, HTTP service, local repository data, and package state. Fixed lifecycle boot identities independently corroborate the restart.","limitations":["The successful transaction proved remote repositories were unavailable to DNF by explicitly disabling them; it did not directly demonstrate a network-layer outage of their endpoints.","The timed-out dead-proxy attempt produced no captured command output, although subsequent evidence showed tree remained absent and the lingering DNF processes were terminated before the successful transaction."]}
